      "writtenOn": "2025-07-21T23:52:54Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "IMPORTANT: This is a preexisting issue. I found that some hashes near the right and bottom borders are calculated but not used.\n\nFor a concrete example, suppose The picture is 16x16, and the current `block_size` is 4. So `src_size` is 2.\n\nConsider the first iteration of the outer for loop. In the last iteration of the inner for loop, `x_pos` is equal to `x_end - 1 \u003d picture-\u003ey_crop_width - block_size \u003d 16 - 4 \u003d 12`. So we read the following entries in `src_pic_block_hash`:\n\n`src_pic_block_hash[pos] \u003d src_pic_block_hash[12]`\n`src_pic_block_hash[pos + src_size] \u003d src_pic_block_hash[14]`\n\nNote that `src_pic_block_hash[13]` and `src_pic_block_hash[15]` are not used. Although `src_pic_block_hash[15]` was not calculated, `src_pic_block_hash[13]` was calculated.\n\nIf we consider the last iteration of the outer for loop, I believe we can show, with a similar argument, that two entire rows of hash values, row index 13 and 15, are not used. Although row index 15 was not calculaed, row index 13 was calculated.\n\nPlease double check my analysis. If you think it is correct, we should think if this is intended and if this is a bug.",
      "revId": "30725b63277a4a0cd2b35217b714aaf285da8dc1",
      "serverId": "e5514cf8-2d6e-3e29-adb4-24cd6dde4bf0"
    },
