      "writtenOn": "2025-07-22T18:53:27Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think this is intended behavior. Following your example, the 2x2 hashes for `src_pic_block_hash[13]` and `src_pic_block_hash[15]` are not part of the 4x4 block we\u0027re currently hashing, but to potential neighboring 4x4 blocks (with coordinates shifted 1 pixel to the left or right).\n\nAdditionally, due to the way the code is written, intraBC block references cannot come from partially outside the image. `src_pic_block_hash[13]` is part of the second-to-last 4x4 block (i.e. [pos - 1 + src_size]), while `src_pic_block_hash[15]` cannot be part of any larger block.\n\nHope this explains what\u0027s happening. I added a comment so the behavior is clearer.",
      "parentUuid": "9cd08def_7671f64c",
      "revId": "30725b63277a4a0cd2b35217b714aaf285da8dc1",
      "serverId": "e5514cf8-2d6e-3e29-adb4-24cd6dde4bf0"
