      "message": "Wan-Teh: I found out why the `+ 1` for both width and height are necessary here. It\u0027s because there will always be `picture-\u003ey_crop_width - width + 1` by `picture-\u003ey_crop_height - height + 1` blocks of size `width x height` to process.\n\nExample, for an image of size 8x8, and block size 4x4:\n```\n- picture-\u003ey_crop_width 8\n- width 4\n- x_end 5\n\n- picture-\u003ey_crop_height 8\n- height 4\n- y_end 5\n```\n\n`x_pos` will then have a range `[0-4]`, and `y_pos` will have a range `[0-4]`. So that\u0027s 5 x 5 values along each axis \u003d 25 total 4x4 block candidates.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 249,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 250,
        "endChar": 48
      },
